OpenCMIS Android Client
=======================

The OpenCMIS Android Client provides a collection of methods to access and
manage a CMIS repository from mobile / constrained environments.


OpenCMIS Client Bindings supported
----------------------------------
AtomPub Binding and Browser Binding are supported.
The Web Service Binding (SOAP) is not supported.


Runtime / build notes
---------------------
 - This module no longer depends on `com.google.android:android` stubs.
   XML parsing uses XmlPull via `net.sf.kxml:kxml2`.
 - The artifact is compiled with `--release 11` (parent reactor stays on
   Java 21). Consumers should target a modern Android minSdk that can
   run Java 11 bytecode, or recompile with a lower release if needed.
 - Packaging is verified in CI (`package -DskipTests`); there is no
   device/emulator smoke test in this repository.


IMPORTANT: synchronous API
--------------------------
OpenCMIS Android Client is a SYNCHRONOUS library.
Encapsulate CMIS calls in a background thread (Service, Loader,
Executor, Coroutine, etc.).


Maven dependency
----------------

    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.apache.chemistry.opencmis</groupId>
        <artifactId>chemistry-opencmis-android-client</artifactId>
        <version>${opencmis.version}</version>
    </dependency>

Also add an SLF4J Android binding appropriate for your app
(for example `org.slf4j:slf4j-android`).


Code sample
-----------
See the previous Activity / AsyncTask sample in git history, or use
SessionFactoryImpl with AtomPub parameters as in the desktop client
documentation.
